## Implementation

### The Challenge: Server Validation

**Problem:** Server recalculates expected talents on login via `InitTalentForLevel()`:
```cpp
// Player.cpp:2538
void Player::InitTalentForLevel()
{
    uint32 expected = CalculateTalentsPoints();  // Expected based on level
    uint32 used = GetUsedTalentCount();          // Actual spent talents

    if (used > expected)
    {
        resetTalents(true);  // WIPES ALL TALENTS
    }
}
```

**Issue:** Lua hooks fire AFTER this validation. Too late to prevent resets.

If Lua grants bonus points without server knowing, server sees:
- Expected: 19 (level 19, default formula)
- Used: 57 (Lua granted +2 per level)
- Used > Expected → RESET ALL TALENTS

### The Solution: C++ Module + Lua Script

Two-part system:

#### Part 1: mod-talent-bonus (C++)

Hooks `OnPlayerCalculateTalentsPoints` to adjust expected count:
```cpp
class TalentBonusScript : public PlayerScript
{
public:
    void OnPlayerCalculateTalentsPoints(Player* player, uint32 level, uint32& points) override
    {
        // Get XP progress (0.0 to 1.0)
        float progress = GetLevelProgress(player);

        // Add +1 if past 33% threshold
        if (progress >= 0.33f)
            points += 1;

        // Add +1 if past 66% threshold
        if (progress >= 0.66f)
            points += 1;
    }
};
```

**Effect:** Server now **expects** the bonus points. Validation passes.

#### Part 2: levelling.lua (Lua)

Awards actual talent points at thresholds:
```lua
-- src/lua/levelling.lua
RegisterPlayerEvent(PLAYER_EVENT_ON_GIVE_XP, function(event, player, amount, victim)
    local level = player:GetLevel()
    if level >= 20 then return end  -- Max level reached

    local xpForLevel = player:GetUInt32Value(PLAYER_NEXT_LEVEL_XP)
    local currentXP = player:GetUInt32Value(PLAYER_XP)
    local progress = currentXP / xpForLevel

    -- 33% threshold
    if progress >= 0.33 and not player:GetData("talent_33_" .. level) then
        player:SetData("talent_33_" .. level, true)
        player:ModifyTalentPoints(1)  -- Grant +1 talent
        sendGreenLevelUpEffect(player)  -- Visual feedback
    end

    -- 66% threshold
    if progress >= 0.66 and not player:GetData("talent_66_" .. level) then
        player:SetData("talent_66_" .. level, true)
        player:ModifyTalentPoints(1)
        sendGreenLevelUpEffect(player)
    end

    -- 100% (level up) handled by server Rate.Talent = 1
end)
```

**Effect:** Players receive points with visual feedback. Tracking via `SetData()` prevents duplicates.

### Visual Effects

**Green effect (33% and 66%):**
```lua
function sendGreenLevelUpEffect(player)
    -- Uses SMSG_SET_FACTION_STANDING packet
    -- Same visual as "reputation level gained"
